NNAAMMEE
       dpkg-genchanges - generate Debian .changes files

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ddppkkgg--ggeenncchhaannggeess [_o_p_t_i_o_n...]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ddppkkgg--ggeenncchhaannggeess reads information from an unpacked and built Debian
       source tree and from the files it has generated and generates a Debian
       upload control file (..cchhaannggeess file).

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       ----bbuuiilldd==_t_y_p_e
           Specifies the build _t_y_p_e from a comma-separated list of components
           (since dpkg 1.18.5).

           The allowed values are:

           ssoouurrccee
               Upload the source package.

           aannyy Upload the architecture specific binary packages.

           aallll Upload the architecture independent binary packages.

           bbiinnaarryy
               Upload the architecture specific and independent binary
               packages.  This is an alias for aannyy,,aallll.

           ffuullll
               Upload everything.  This is alias for ssoouurrccee,,aannyy,,aallll, and the
               same as the default case when no build option is specified.

       --gg  Equivalent to ----bbuuiilldd==ssoouurrccee,,aallll (since dpkg 1.17.11).

       --GG  Equivalent to ----bbuuiilldd==ssoouurrccee,,aannyy (since dpkg 1.17.11).

       --bb  Equivalent to ----bbuuiilldd==bbiinnaarryy or ----bbuuiilldd==aannyy,,aallll.

       --BB  Equivalent to ----bbuuiilldd==aannyy.

       --AA  Equivalent to ----bbuuiilldd==aallll.

       --SS  Equivalent to ----bbuuiilldd==ssoouurrccee.

       The --ss_x options control whether the original source archive is included
       in the upload if any source is being generated (i.e.  --bb or --BB haven't
       been used).

       --ssii By default, or if specified, the original source will be included
           only if the upstream version number (the version without epoch and
           without Debian revision) differs from the upstream version number
           of the previous changelog entry.

       --ssaa Forces the inclusion of the original source.

       --ssdd Forces the exclusion of the original source and includes only the
           diff.

       --vv_v_e_r_s_i_o_n
